The Angular build is consuming all available JS heap before it can produce output, even with a large max-old-space-size. That is the same outcome on both production and development configurations, so this is not a configuration choice — it is a build-environment capacity problem.

Before I decide how to treat this, I should confirm the actual Node and Angular CLI versions the build is running with, because the OOM behavior may be worse than the project intends and worth documenting precisely rather than inferring.
