That `ng build --configuration development --aot=false` run is far more useful than the OOM noise: it surfaced a real frontend defect, not an environment-only failure. The Angular compiler is rejecting multiple `@angular/common` and `@angular/common/http` imports because the installed package metadata/types are inconsistent, and the actual API service also has type-safety bugs that would break in a working build.

I'll patch the frontend typing/config issue first, then re-run the dev build to see whether it gets past compilation or whether there's a deeper node_modules integrity problem.
